From f1acd36b4961524ce3a94511a205b43ecd370293 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kelebek <berkantkelebek2@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 19:06:16 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 02/13] DirectStorage: inflate zlib requests (file and memory
 sources)

A request with ZlibDecompress alone now reads SourceSize bytes of the file or of memory into a staging buffer,
inflates them with the runtime's RFC 1950 inflater (leonida::zlib_inflate in src/shader_library.h) and copies the
result to Destination only when it is exactly DestinationSize bytes. A failed stream leaves the destination
untouched, and a memory source inside its own destination inflates correctly.

Checks follow DSTORAGE_REQUEST and dstorageerr.h: DestinationSize must be larger than SourceSize with zlib
(E_DSTORAGE_INVALID_DESTINATION_SIZE), a zlib FileOffset must be 16-byte aligned (E_DSTORAGE_INVALID_FILE_OFFSET),
IntermediateSize stays 0 without BCPack. Stream failures map to E_DSTORAGE_ZLIB_BAD_HEADER, _ZLIB_BAD_DATA,
_ZLIB_PARITY_FAIL (Adler-32) and E_DSTORAGE_DECOMPRESSION_ERROR (a result of another size). GetStats counts
the inflates, the pending ones and the decompression errors.

zlib_inflate gains an optional failure reason (header, data, checksum, limit); its existing callers are unchanged.
BCPack, swizzle and physical-page requests still fail with E_NOTIMPL.

dstorage_test: synthetic streams only (Python zlib levels 9 and 1, stored blocks built by the test), from a file
and from memory, with every failure code; shader_library_test checks the new failure reasons.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
